  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n** x+(1)/(x)=(K)/(2)**\n\n**Concept Used:**\n\n** x+(1)/(x)=a**, then\n\n x²+(1)/(x²)=a² - 2\n\n x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=[x²-(1)/(x²)]² - 2\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n x+(1)/(x)=(K)/(2)\n\n⇒ x²+(1)/(x²)=(K²)/(4) - 2\n\n⇒ x²+(1)/(x²)=(K² - 8)/(4)\n\n⇒ x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=[(K² - 8)/(4)]² - 2\n\n⇒ x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=[(K⁴ + 64 - 16K²)/(16)] - 2\n\n⇒ x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=[(K⁴ + 32 - 16K²)/(16)] \n\n**∴ Option 1 is the correct answer.**",
